Editor art and the scripts that generate it (gui/, resources/img/):

  Copyright (c) 2026 rations — MIT Licence.

  The amp-head panel (head-base.png), the speaker cabinet (cabinet-base.png),
  the dial and the indicator lamps are the author's own artwork. The bat-handle
  toggle switches (switch_up_ring.png, switch_down_ring.png) and the meter track
  are generated procedurally by gui/make_switch.sh and gui/make_meter.sh
  (ImageMagick 7) rather than authored as raster files, and Folder.svg is the
  author's own, drawn to match the icon set below. There is no badge image: the
  "Rations" wordmark is drawn as text in Michroma at run time.

  gui/make_knob.sh, and gui/make_switch.sh's ancestor make_footswitch.sh, were
  originally written by the same author for a sibling project that is licensed
  GPL-3.0-or-later, and they carried that project's GPL-3 header. That project
  is GPL-3 solely because it links JUCE. Neither script contains JUCE code or
  derives from anything GPL-licensed: both are pure ImageMagick 7 command
  pipelines (masks, radial gradients, and the CopyOpacity / DstIn / screen
  compose operators), and the only mention of JUCE in either file was a comment
  explaining why the knob art must be trimmed and centred before rotation — a
  requirement that applies identically to Cairo. As the sole author and
  copyright holder, the author has relicensed them MIT for use here.

